### Problem description
Copy-paste bug in `moreh_layer_norm_backward_gamma_beta_grad_program_factory.cpp`: the guard for writing `beta_grad_buffer->address()` into runtime args checks `gamma_grad_buffer != nullptr` instead of `beta_grad_buffer != nullptr`. When `gamma_grad_buffer` is non-null but `beta_grad_buffer` is null (i.e. only `gamma_grad` is requested), this is a null pointer dereference — caught by Clang Static Analyzer (`core.CallAndMessage`).

### What's changed
- **One-line fix**: changed the condition on line 302 from `gamma_grad_buffer != nullptr` → `beta_grad_buffer != nullptr`.

```cpp
// Before
if (gamma_grad_buffer != nullptr) {
    runtime_args[1] = beta_grad_buffer->address();  // NPE when beta_grad_buffer is null
}

// After
if (beta_grad_buffer != nullptr) {
    runtime_args[1] = beta_grad_buffer->address();
}
```

