Three type groups were independently redefined across feature slices, violating D19 (cross-BC contracts belong in `shared-kernel`) and D20 (import priority: `shared-kernel` > slice index > `shared/types`).

## Changes

- **`shared-kernel/index.ts`** — export `Location` from `schedule-contract`; it was already defined there but never surfaced at the kernel boundary
- **`business.tasks/_types.ts`** — drop local `Location` interface; import from `@/features/shared-kernel` and re-export for backward compatibility
- **`business.document-parser/_types.ts`** — remove duplicate `ParsingIntentSourceType` / `ParsingIntentReviewStatus` definitions; import from the authoritative `business.parsing-intent/_contract`; replace inline `status` union with the named `ParsingIntentStatus` type
- **`business.parsing-intent/index.ts`** — add `ParsingIntentSourceType` and `ParsingIntentReviewStatus` to public exports so consumers reach them via the slice boundary

```ts
// Before — identical union defined in two places
// business.document-parser/_types.ts
export type ParsingIntentSourceType = 'ai' | 'human' | 'system';

// business.parsing-intent/_contract.ts
export type ParsingIntentSourceType = 'ai' | 'human' | 'system';

// After — single source of truth in _contract; _types.ts re-exports
import type { ParsingIntentSourceType, ParsingIntentReviewStatus, ParsingIntentStatus }
  from '../business.parsing-intent/_contract';
export type { ParsingIntentSourceType, ParsingIntentReviewStatus };
```

