The Supabase join result for the `clients` relation was cast to `as any`, bypassing type safety on the `client` object used throughout the email-sending logic.

## Changes

- **New interfaces** — `ClientRecord` and `JobWithClient` describe the exact shape of the join query result
- **`.returns<T>()` on query** — Supabase's generic override method replaces the unsafe cast; TypeScript now infers the correct type from the SDK itself
- **Removed** — `as any`, the explanatory workaround comment, and the `eslint-disable` directive

```ts
// Before
const client = job.client as any;

// After
interface ClientRecord { name: string; email: string; }
interface JobWithClient {
  id: string; title: string; contractor_id: string;
  client: ClientRecord | null;
}

const { data: job } = await supabase
  .from("jobs")
  .select(`id, title, contractor_id, client:clients (name, email)`)
  .returns<JobWithClient>()
  .single();

const client = job.client; // fully typed, no assertion
```

