The email body frame showed horizontal scrollbars on messages that didn’t fit the viewport; mobile users had to pan to read.

- **Responsive container**: Email container now stays within the viewport (`max-width: 100%`) while allowing horizontal overflow only when absolutely necessary (`overflow-x: auto`).
- **Shadow wrapper width**: Shadow DOM wrapper fills and matches the container width, promoting natural wrapping to avoid scrollbars on mobile and desktop.
- **Accessibility preserved**: Horizontal overflow is no longer forcibly hidden, keeping wide content reachable while relying on wrapping first.

